But in this case, the discriminant is zero. However, since there's only x² term and no y² term, so when discriminant is zero, and there's only one squared term, it would be a parabola. If there were both x² and y² terms, and discriminant zero, it could be a parabola or a degenerate case. But in this case, since there is exactly one squared term, it is a parabola.

