### Step 1: Use the identity for cosine equality

The identity for when two cosine values are equal is:
$$
\cos A = \cos B \iff A = B + 360^\circ k \quad \text{or} \quad A = -B + 360^\circ k \quad \text{for some integer } k
$$

Applying this to the given problem:
